('127.681.d.6.E',4,'A crimping tool is used to:','["measure voltage", "attach connectors to cable ends", "paint walls", "cut wood"]'::jsonb,1,'Crimpers fasten RJ-45 plugs.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.F',3,'A patch is a:','["kind of router", "type of cable", "small update that fixes a problem in software", "screen cover"]'::jsonb,2,'Patches fix bugs.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.F',4,'Before applying a vendor fix to a production network device, a technician should read the:','["menu", "advertisement", "calendar", "release notes and test if possible"]'::jsonb,3,'Notes describe changes and risks.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.G',3,'A backup copy kept off-site helps protect data from:','["fire or theft at the main location", "a dirty screen", "a loose chair", "slow typing"]'::jsonb,0,'Off-site copies survive local disasters.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.G',4,'A common good practice is to follow the 3-2-1 rule, which means keeping:','["two copies on one drive", "three copies on two kinds of media with one off-site", "one copy in one place", "no copies"]'::jsonb,1,'3-2-1 spreads risk.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.H',3,'Which can slow a network?','["a new switch", "a short cable", "too many users sharing limited bandwidth", "a quiet room"]'::jsonb,2,'Congestion reduces speed.','original'),
('127.681.d.6.H',4,'A very long cable run beyond the standard distance limit can cause:','["no change", "stronger signals", "faster speeds", "signal loss and errors"]'::jsonb,3,'Distance weakens signals.','original'),
('127.681.d.7.A',3,'A recovery plan for a network should state how to restore:','["critical services and data after an outage", "office music", "vending machines", "parking lots"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans focus on restoring operations.','original'),
('127.681.d.7.A',4,'In a recovery plan, the most important systems are usually restored:','["last", "first", "at random", "never"]'::jsonb,1,'Critical systems are prioritized.','original'),
('127.681.d.7.B',3,'A maintenance plan for network devices might schedule:','["office parties", "paint jobs", "firmware updates and cable checks", "furniture moves"]'::jsonb,2,'Planned upkeep prevents failures.','original'),
('127.681.d.7.B',4,'Keeping a maintenance log helps the team:','["hide tasks", "skip checks", "avoid planning", "see what was done and when"]'::jsonb,3,'Logs track maintenance history.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.A',3,'A telecommunications technician who is dependable and shows initiative is more likely to:','["keep their job and move up", "get fewer tasks", "be ignored", "lose their badge"]'::jsonb,0,'Strong work habits support advancement.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.A',4,'Which is a work behavior employers value in a cable installer?','["rushing sloppy work", "completing jobs on schedule with attention to detail", "skipping safety checks", "arriving whenever convenient"]'::jsonb,1,'Quality and timeliness matter.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.B',3,'A person who adjusts easily when job plans change shows:','["stubbornness", "indifference", "flexibility", "carelessness"]'::jsonb,2,'Flexibility helps in changing work.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.B',4,'Open-mindedness during a team troubleshooting session means you:','["refuse to test anything", "dismiss all ideas", "talk over teammates", "listen to others'' theories before deciding"]'::jsonb,3,'Open-minded teams find causes faster.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.C',3,'A network installer reading the wiring standard before starting is:','["using reading skills to prevent errors", "wasting time", "ignoring the work order", "delaying the job"]'::jsonb,0,'Reading prevents mistakes.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.C',4,'A well-written incident report should state:','["opinions only", "what happened, when and what was done", "a guess of blame", "jokes"]'::jsonb,1,'Reports must be factual.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.D',3,'Speaking clearly to a client about an outage and when it will be fixed shows:','["laziness", "poor planning", "good verbal communication", "rudeness"]'::jsonb,2,'Clear speech informs the client.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.D',4,'A technician crosses their arms, frowns and looks away while a client explains a problem. This nonverbal signal suggests:','["agreement", "excitement", "careful listening", "disinterest"]'::jsonb,3,'Body language can signal attitude.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.E',3,'A network is slow. A good first problem-solving step is to:','["identify when and where the slowdown happens", "blame the users", "restart everything blindly", "buy new equipment"]'::jsonb,0,'Defining the problem comes first.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.E',4,'Critical thinking during troubleshooting includes:','["skipping tests", "forming a theory and testing it", "assuming the first guess", "copying someone else''s answer"]'::jsonb,1,'Theories need testing.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.F',3,'On a cable installation crew, leadership may include:','["hiding the plan", "ignoring the crew", "helping coworkers stay on schedule and safe", "taking all breaks"]'::jsonb,2,'Leaders support the team.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.F',4,'A team member who finishes early and offers to help others is:','["wasting time", "breaking rules", "showing off", "contributing to the team''s success"]'::jsonb,3,'Teamwork improves outcomes.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.G',3,'When working on an overhead cable run, a technician should use a:','["stable ladder rated for the work", "wobbly chair", "desk on wheels", "stack of boxes"]'::jsonb,0,'Proper ladders prevent falls.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.G',4,'Before handling fiber-optic cable ends, a technician should wear:','["sunglasses only", "safety glasses", "earmuffs", "no protection"]'::jsonb,1,'Fiber shards can injure eyes.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.H',3,'Using a coworker''s login to access company data without permission is:','["required", "harmless", "unethical and may be illegal", "encouraged"]'::jsonb,2,'Unauthorized access breaks policy and law.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.H',4,'A technician working on a client''s network sees confidential files. The ethical choice is to:','["read them for fun", "copy them", "sell them", "not open or share them"]'::jsonb,3,'Confidentiality must be kept.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.I',3,'A project schedule helps a team by showing:','["what must be done and by when", "lunch choices", "what music is playing", "who won a game"]'::jsonb,0,'Schedules coordinate work.','original'),
('127.682.d.1.I',4,'If a cabling job will take two days, the team should plan tasks in:','["reverse order only", "logical order with time for testing", "random order", "no order"]'::jsonb,1,'Order and testing time prevent rework.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.A',3,'To learn about a job as a network installer, a student could:','["watch a cartoon", "play a game", "interview someone who does that job", "guess"]'::jsonb,2,'Interviews give direct information.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.A',4,'Information about a job''s wages and outlook can be found from:','["a joke website", "a rumor", "an advertisement for sneakers", "the Bureau of Labor Statistics"]'::jsonb,3,'BLS publishes job data.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.B',3,'A career plan should include:','["goals and the steps to reach them", "nothing", "random ideas", "only wishes"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans connect goals to actions.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.B',4,'Adding a certification to a plan helps show:','["a change of subject", "progress toward a specific job qualification", "a lack of direction", "wasted time"]'::jsonb,1,'Certifications are milestones.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.C',3,'Which description fits a strong resume for a job application?','["handwritten in pencil", "exaggerated", "accurate, neat and free of errors", "messy"]'::jsonb,2,'Resumes should be correct.','original'),
('127.682.d.2.C',4,'When applying for a telecom job, tailor your resume by:','["using a long paragraph", "hiding your contact data", "listing every job you ever wanted", "emphasizing skills related to the posting"]'::jsonb,3,'Tailoring improves match.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.A',3,'When a customer reports ''the internet is down,'' a technician should:','["ask questions to learn what exactly is not working", "hang up", "change the router at once", "assume the cause"]'::jsonb,0,'Questions define the problem.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.A',4,'In a written network change request, the writer should state the:','["office color", "reason for the change and the expected effect", "lunch plans", "writer''s hobbies"]'::jsonb,1,'Requests explain purpose and impact.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.B',3,'A work order for a new cable run might include the:','["holiday schedule", "customer''s favorite movie", "location and type of cable to install", "technician''s age"]'::jsonb,2,'Specifics guide the work.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.B',4,'Closing out a work order means:','["hiding it", "ignoring it", "throwing it away", "recording completion and any issues found"]'::jsonb,3,'Closure documents the result.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.C',3,'Materials for a cabling job are estimated by:','["measuring distances and counting connectors", "guessing wildly", "skipping the survey", "asking for a bigger truck"]'::jsonb,0,'Measurement leads to accurate estimates.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.C',4,'A job needs 300 feet of cable at $0.40 per foot and 20 connectors at $0.75 each. What is the material cost?','["$120", "$135", "$150", "$115"]'::jsonb,1,'120 + 15 = 135.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.D',3,'A wiring chart used by installers shows:','["car models", "pay rates", "which wires go to which pins", "employee names"]'::jsonb,2,'Charts show connections.','original'),
('127.682.d.3.D',4,'Interpreting a diagram incorrectly during installation could cause:','["a faster network", "fewer costs", "more security", "a network connection that does not work"]'::jsonb,3,'Errors lead to faults.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.A',3,'Analyzing a network starts with identifying its:','["devices, cables and connections", "clocks", "chairs", "paint colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Analysis starts with components.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.A',4,'Mapping which devices connect to which switch ports is useful for:','["decorating", "troubleshooting and planning changes", "choosing names", "scheduling meals"]'::jsonb,1,'Maps support management.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.B',3,'A small office with five computers and a printer would most likely use a:','["satellite network only", "global WAN", "single LAN with one switch", "dozens of routers"]'::jsonb,2,'Small needs call for simple designs.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.B',4,'A building with heavy electrical equipment may need:','["decorative cable", "no cable", "thinner cable", "shielded cable to reduce interference"]'::jsonb,3,'Shielding limits noise.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.C',3,'A company wants employees at two offices to share files securely. A suitable solution is a:','["virtual private network (VPN)", "typewriter", "telegraph", "radio"]'::jsonb,0,'VPNs link sites securely.','original'),
('127.682.d.4.C',4,'Scenario-based problems ask you to choose a network solution that fits the:','["most devices owned", "requirements and constraints given", "most colors", "lowest price only"]'::jsonb,1,'Solutions must fit the scenario.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.A',3,'Before installing a network, written plans should include a:','["vacation request", "costume", "diagram of the layout", "lunch list"]'::jsonb,2,'Diagrams guide installation.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.A',4,'A site survey before a network install helps identify:','["office slogans", "team nicknames", "menu choices", "obstacles and the best equipment locations"]'::jsonb,3,'Surveys reveal practical constraints.','original'),
