('127.682.d.5.D',3,'An addressing scheme assigns each device a:','["unique address on the network", "nickname", "paint color", "job title"]'::jsonb,0,'Unique addresses avoid conflicts.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.D',4,'With a /24 subnet, how many bits identify the network portion?','["16", "24", "32", "8"]'::jsonb,1,'A /24 uses 24 network bits.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.E',3,'A tool used to find where a cable is broken is a:','["paintbrush", "spoon", "time-domain reflectometer or cable tester", "calculator only"]'::jsonb,2,'Testers locate cable faults.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.E',4,'A tool for checking whether a cable end is wired to standard is a:','["level", "power drill", "tape measure", "wire map tester"]'::jsonb,3,'Wire map testers verify pin order.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.F',3,'Vendor documents that describe fixes for known issues are called:','["patch notes or release notes", "brochures", "menus", "newsletters"]'::jsonb,0,'Release notes list fixes.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.F',4,'Why read vendor testing documents before upgrading a router?','["to find a coupon", "to confirm the update is compatible and safe", "to waste time", "to avoid the upgrade forever"]'::jsonb,1,'Documentation guards against surprises.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.G',3,'Being aware of backup procedures means knowing:','["the CEO''s lunch", "the vending prices", "what gets backed up and how often", "the parking map"]'::jsonb,2,'Procedures define backup scope and timing.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.G',4,'Storing backup tapes in a locked, fireproof safe protects them from:','["traffic", "noise", "boredom", "theft and fire"]'::jsonb,3,'Storage practices protect backup media.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.H',3,'The cable most associated with lower cost and easy installation in offices is:','["unshielded twisted pair", "coaxial from a satellite", "phone cord", "glass fiber"]'::jsonb,0,'UTP is cheap and flexible.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.H',4,'A cable best suited for very long, high-speed runs between buildings is:','["flat patch cord", "fiber-optic cable", "extension cord", "speaker wire"]'::jsonb,1,'Fiber carries data far at high speed.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.I',3,'Network performance can be reduced by:','["new equipment", "low use", "outdated equipment and heavy traffic", "short cables"]'::jsonb,2,'Old gear and congestion slow networks.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.I',4,'Adding a second access point in a large office may improve:','["paper supply", "parking", "lighting", "wireless coverage and capacity"]'::jsonb,3,'More access points spread the load.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.J',3,'Staying aware of new telecommunications technology means:','["reading about changes in the industry", "ignoring trends", "avoiding news", "deleting emails"]'::jsonb,0,'Awareness keeps skills current.','original'),
('127.682.d.5.J',4,'A technician hears that a new wireless standard has launched. A good move is to:','["ignore it", "study its features and where it fits", "delete all notes", "laugh"]'::jsonb,1,'Learning prepares you for change.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.A',3,'Before mixing old and new network equipment, a technician should check:','["the logos", "the box sizes", "whether the devices are compatible", "the colors"]'::jsonb,2,'Compatibility prevents failures.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.A',4,'Cat5e cable cannot support the highest speeds that Cat6a can. This is a:','["paint issue", "font issue", "software update", "cabling limitation"]'::jsonb,3,'Cable category limits speed.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.B',3,'An address like 192.168.1.20 is an example of:','["an IPv4 address", "a street address", "a phone number", "a web page"]'::jsonb,0,'IPv4 addresses use four numbers.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.B',4,'Putting a lab network and an office network on different subnets:','["removes addresses", "keeps their traffic separate", "slows power", "merges all traffic"]'::jsonb,1,'Subnets isolate groups.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.C',3,'When installing data connectors, the technician should follow the:','["recipe", "alphabet", "wiring standard, such as T568B", "phone book"]'::jsonb,2,'Standards ensure consistent wiring.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.C',4,'Which tool strips the outer jacket from a network cable?','["a hammer", "a saw", "a ruler", "a cable stripper"]'::jsonb,3,'Strippers remove jackets without nicking wires.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.D',3,'After attaching a connector to a cable, the technician should:','["test the cable before using it", "hide it", "paint it", "throw it away"]'::jsonb,0,'Testing confirms a good connection.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.D',4,'Connecting a patch cable between a wall jack and a computer completes the:','["screen display", "path to the network", "lunch order", "power supply"]'::jsonb,1,'The patch cable links device and jack.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.E',3,'A link light on a network port that stays off usually indicates:','["a fast network", "a printing job", "no connection is detected", "a happy user"]'::jsonb,2,'No link light means no signal.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.E',4,'Blinking lights on a switch port typically show:','["a missing cable", "a power cut", "a broken screen", "data activity"]'::jsonb,3,'Blinking indicates traffic.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.F',3,'Troubleshooting should follow a:','["systematic approach", "skipping approach", "random approach", "guessing approach"]'::jsonb,0,'A method avoids missed steps.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.F',4,'If all users lose access but the problem is not at their desks, the fault is probably:','["each monitor", "a shared device or the internet link", "each user''s mouse", "each chair"]'::jsonb,1,'Shared failures point to shared parts.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.G',3,'Once a problem''s cause is found, the next step is to:','["guess again", "blame someone", "choose and apply the best fix", "ignore the cause"]'::jsonb,2,'Corrective action follows diagnosis.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.G',4,'After applying a fix, a technician should:','["leave quickly", "hide the issue", "skip documentation", "verify that the problem is resolved"]'::jsonb,3,'Verification confirms the fix.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.H',3,'Organizing network files into folders by department helps users:','["find and manage data more easily", "lose files", "avoid sharing", "slow the drive"]'::jsonb,0,'Hierarchies improve organization.','original'),
('127.682.d.6.H',4,'Setting folder permissions so only one team can edit a folder protects:','["the speaker", "the integrity of the team''s data", "the monitor", "the room"]'::jsonb,1,'Permissions control changes.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.A',3,'A security threat to an information system could be:','["a sunny day", "a new chair", "malware or unauthorized access", "a quiet hallway"]'::jsonb,2,'Threats harm systems or data.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.A',4,'Assessing security threats begins with identifying the:','["parking spaces", "lunch breaks", "office decorations", "assets that need protection"]'::jsonb,3,'You must know what to protect.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.B',3,'A common problem on a data network is:','["unauthorized users trying to gain access", "too short a cable", "too much quiet", "too many windows"]'::jsonb,0,'Access control is a core concern.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.B',4,'Weak passwords create a security need for:','["new chairs", "password policies and multi-factor sign-in", "longer breaks", "more paint"]'::jsonb,1,'Policies and extra factors reduce risk.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.C',3,'Using someone else''s network without permission is considered:','["a requirement", "a harmless game", "unethical and often illegal", "a service"]'::jsonb,2,'Unauthorized use is wrongdoing.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.C',4,'Downloading and sharing paid music or movies without permission is called:','["file backup", "email", "cloud storage", "online piracy"]'::jsonb,3,'Piracy violates copyright.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.D',3,'The right to control who sees your personal data is called:','["privacy", "publicity", "speed", "bandwidth"]'::jsonb,0,'Privacy protects personal information.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.D',4,'A debate over how much the government should monitor communications involves balancing security and:','["cable color", "privacy rights", "screen size", "font choice"]'::jsonb,1,'This tension is central to policy.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.E',3,'A network security plan should be:','["kept secret from everyone", "never updated", "written down and shared with those responsible", "lost"]'::jsonb,2,'Written plans guide action.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.E',4,'Implementing a security plan includes training users on:','["game scores", "new wallpaper", "office decor", "safe practices such as spotting phishing emails"]'::jsonb,3,'Users are part of security.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.F',3,'A firewall helps secure a network by:','["filtering traffic according to rules", "cooling devices", "printing pages", "storing files"]'::jsonb,0,'Firewalls allow or block traffic.','original'),
('127.682.d.7.F',4,'An intrusion detection system watches the network and:','["prints invoices", "alerts staff to suspicious activity", "paints walls", "adds RAM"]'::jsonb,1,'IDS tools detect threats.','original'),
('127.682.d.8.A',3,'When pulling cable through a ceiling, a technician should avoid:','["using a ladder", "wearing gloves", "touching power lines and unsupported ceiling tiles", "turning on a light"]'::jsonb,2,'Ceilings can hide hazards.','original'),
('127.682.d.8.A',4,'Which safety item should be worn when drilling into a wall to run cable?','["a scarf", "slippers", "a watch", "eye protection"]'::jsonb,3,'Debris can injure eyes.','original'),
('127.682.d.8.B',3,'Old network equipment like routers and batteries should be:','["recycled through an approved electronics program", "burned", "left outside", "tossed in the trash"]'::jsonb,0,'E-waste needs proper disposal.','original'),
('127.682.d.8.B',4,'The document that explains how to handle a hazardous material safely is the:','["receipt", "Safety Data Sheet", "menu", "brochure"]'::jsonb,1,'SDS provides handling details.','original'),
('127.682.d.9.A',3,'Recovery plans for a telecom center should say what to do if:','["a chair breaks", "a lunch is late", "power or a major link fails", "a pen runs out"]'::jsonb,2,'Plans cover major outages.','original'),
('127.682.d.9.A',4,'A recovery plan should be tested by:','["ignoring drills", "hiding it", "never reading it", "practicing the steps before a real emergency"]'::jsonb,3,'Testing finds gaps.','original'),
('127.682.d.9.B',3,'Replacing worn cables before they fail is part of:','["preventive maintenance", "sales", "guesswork", "neglect"]'::jsonb,0,'Preventive work avoids failures.','original'),
('127.682.d.9.B',4,'A preventive maintenance schedule for a telecom closet might include:','["unplugging devices", "regular inspections and cleaning of equipment", "leaving doors open", "adding clutter"]'::jsonb,1,'Routine checks catch problems early.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
